    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/CBB2694288FE9606215883F78F64E0A2/jobs/176618": {
      "title": "Program Manager for Career Readiness",
      "description": "Program Manager for Career Readiness You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Program Manager for Career Readiness Newberry College - Newberry, SC 29108 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply Description The Program Manager for Career Readiness leads the implementation, integration, assessment, and continuous improvement of the Career Ready Guide and approved related career readiness initiatives. Working directly with designated student populations and in collaboration with faculty, academic programs, student-support offices, and campus partners, the Program Manager integrates career planning, goal-setting, and workforce readiness into curricular and co-curricular experiences. Through faculty support and data-informed program development, the position helps students recognize, develop, and communicate the competencies needed for academic, professional, and post-graduate success. The position provides individualized career coaching, proactive outreach, and career readiness programming to assigned student populations. The Program Manager plans and carries out this work in coordination with the Director of the Muller Center for Careers & Purpose, ensuring that priorities, content, timelines, student-engagement strategies, and program development remain aligned with Center priorities, grant objectives, established program goals, and institutional needs. JOB FUNCTIONS: Program Implementation and Curricular Integration Lead implementation and ongoing coordination of the Career Ready Guide and related initiatives. Coordinate the integration of career readiness into first-year and transfer experiences. Build collaborative relationships with faculty, course coordinators, academic departments, and student-support offices. Develop faculty implementation plans, communication materials, instructional resources, classroom activities, and assessment tools. Provide faculty and staff training and implementation support. Student Coaching, Programming, and Outreach Provide student-facing coaching, workshops, classroom presentations, and group learning experiences. Develop outreach and engagement strategies for first-year, transfer, and other assigned populations. Facilitate career planning, goal-setting, and workforce-readiness activities. Coordinate cohort-based career readiness programming for first-year and transfer students, including workshops, classroom activities, and related events. Program Direction and Center Collaboration Develop program design recommendations focused on increasing students' use of career readiness competencies. Collaborate with the Program Manager for Career Development Technologies and the Career Development Specialist to align outreach, coaching, technology-supported resources, classroom engagement, and referrals. Assessment and Continuous Improvement Monitor participation, completion, engagement, and outcome data. Develop and administer assessment processes. Collect, analyze, and communicate project data and implementation findings for grant reporting, institutional decision-making, and continuous improvement. Gather feedback to inform improvements to the initiative. Maintain program documentation and standard operating procedures. Remain current on career-readiness frameworks, student development, workforce expectations, and career education. Participate in committees, grant activities, and professional development. Perform other duties as assigned. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION This is a full-time, grant-funded position. The work schedule will be established in coordination with the Director of the Muller Center for Careers & Purpose and may vary based on implementation needs and the College's academic calendar. Occasional evening and weekend hours may be required for training, student programming, campus events, and outreach activities . Qualifications Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in higher education, career development, student affairs, counseling, education, workforce development, human resources, communication, business, or a related field. Experience in career services, academic advising, student success, workforce development, counseling, education, or a related field. Experience working directly with students through coaching, advising, teaching, training, workshops, program facilitation, or related student-development activities. Experience supporting program implementation, including coordinating activities, managing timelines, developing resources, communicating with stakeholders, and following through on commitments. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and campus partners and to build productive relationships across academic and administrative areas. Ability to collect, interpret, and communicate participation, learning, and outcome data for program assessment, reporting, and continuous improvement. Strong interpersonal, written, verbal, facilitation, and presentation skills, including the ability to communicate career readiness concepts clearly to varied audiences. Demonstrated project management and organizational skills, including the ability to balance student-facing work with planning, documentation, assessment, and multiple concurrent priorities. Ability to exercise sound judgment within established priorities and decision-making structures, recognizing when issues, risks, recommendations, or proposed changes require consultation or approval. Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle student and institutional information responsibly while supporting a diverse student population through inclusive, student-centered practices. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in higher education, student affairs, career development, counseling, education, workforce development, human resources, communication, business, or a related discipline. Experience in college career services, first-year experience, academic advising, student success, workforce development, or a related higher education environment. Experience integrating career readiness, student success, or developmental learning activities into courses or co-curricular programs. Familiarity with career readiness competencies and frameworks, particularly approaches that help students identify, develop, reflect on, and communicate employability competencies. Experience designing and delivering faculty, staff, or student training and developing facilitator guides, assignments, presentations, learning resources, or assessment tools. Experience with student outreach, communications, public relations, or marketing that supports program awareness, participation, and engagement. Experience with data visualization, program assessment, learning outcomes, or grant-supported initiatives. APPLICATION Application review will begin immediately and will continue until a candidate is selected. Candidates should submit: Cover letter expressing interest in the position, resume, and list of three professional reference via email to human.resources@newberry.edu with the Subject Line: Program Manager for Career Readiness. Newberry College does not discriminate against any person or group on the basis of age, color, disability, gender, pregnancy, national origin, race, religion, sexual orientation, veteran status or genetic information. Newberry College is building a culturally diverse faculty and staff committed to working in a multicultural environment and encourages applications from people from diverse identities and backgrounds. E-Verify: Currently the college uses E-Verify for employment verification. E-Verify is an internet-based system that compares information entered by an employer from a n employee’s Form I-9 (Employment Eligibility Verification) to records available to the US Department of Homeland Security and the Social Security Administration to confirm employment eligibility. College Employment Policy This job description reflects the general details considered necessary to describe the principal functions of the job identified and shall not necessarily be construed as a detailed description of all the work requirements that may be inherent in the job.  Job descriptions do not constitute an employment agreement or contract of employment, expressed or implied. Unless designated in writing and signed by the College President, all College employees are considered to be “EMPLOYED AT WILL.” Newberry College reserves the right to change, alter and amend job descriptions, functions and duties at the pleasure of the College President or Board of Trustees. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/CBB2694288FE9606215883F78F64E0A2/jobs/176608": {
      "title": "Program Manager for Career Development Technologies",
      "description": "Program Manager for Career Development Technologies You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Program Manager for Career Development Technologies Newberry College - Newberry, SC 29108 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level 4 Year Degree Apply Description The Program Manager for Career Development Technologies oversees designated career development technologies. Working directly with students and in collaboration with faculty, academic programs, information technology staff, vendors, and campus partners, the Program Manager integrates these resources into coursework and career preparation activities and expands access to scalable career development services. Through technology-supported coaching, training, outreach, and assessment, the position strengthens students' career planning, workforce readiness, and preparation for post-graduate opportunities. The position provides individualized career coaching, proactive outreach, and career readiness programming to assigned student populations. The Program Manager plans and carries out this work in coordination with the Director of the Muller Center for Careers & Purpose, ensuring that priorities, platform use, implementation activities, and program development remain aligned with Center priorities, grant objectives, established program goals, and institutional needs. JOB FUNCTIONS: Technology Implementation and Administration Lead implementation and ongoing administration of designated career development technologies, including Big Interview and Big Resume. Manage daily technology operations, platform settings, user access, content, workflows, and user support. Support the evaluation and implementation of additional approved career-planning and goal-setting technologies. Develop and maintain implementation and training documentation and standard operating procedures. Program Direction, Vendor Coordination, and Institutional Collaboration Develop recommendations for platform configuration, expansion, and improvement. Serve as the primary operational contact for vendors and internal partners. Collaborate with information technology and institutional offices on access, integrations, privacy, security, accessibility, and compliance. Faculty Support and Student Engagement Build relationships with faculty and academic programs. Identify opportunities to integrate technologies into courses and co-curricular experiences. Develop faculty and staff implementation and training materials. Provide faculty and staff training and support. Develop and provide student coaching, workshops, training, and classroom presentations that use career development technologies to strengthen resume development, interview preparation, career planning, and career decision-making. Develop student outreach and technology-adoption strategies . Assessment and Continuous Improvement Monitor utilization, participation, completion, and outcome data, maintaining accurate records and dashboards and identifying trends, implementation barriers, and opportunities to improve student engagement and program effectiveness. Collect, analyze, and communicate project data and implementation findings for grant reporting, institutional assessment, decision-making, and continuous improvement. Prepare timely updates and recommendations for the Director. Gather feedback to inform improvements to the initiative. Remain current on career development, educational technology, artificial intelligence, and vendor capabilities. Participate in committees, grant activities, and professional development. Perform other duties as assigned. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION This is a full-time, grant-funded position. The work schedule will be established in coordination with the Director of the Muller Center for Careers & Purpose and may vary based on implementation needs and the College's academic calendar. Occasional evening and weekend hours may be required for training, student programming, campus events, and outreach activities. Qualifications Bachelor's degree in higher education, career development, educational technology, instructional design, student affairs, business, communication, information systems, or a related field. Experience supporting technology-based programs or services, including implementation, user training, system administration, customer support, or related responsibilities. Experience working directly with students or other users in career development, workforce development, higher education, student success, training, or a related setting. Demonstrated project management and organizational skills, including the ability to coordinate multiple stakeholders, manage timelines, document processes, identify risks, and follow through on commitments. Ability to collect, interpret, and communicate participation and outcome data for program assessment, reporting, and continuous improvement. Strong interpersonal, written, verbal, and presentation skills, including the ability to train users, facilitate workshops, explain technology clearly, and build effective relationships with students, faculty, staff, vendors, and campus partners. Ability to exercise sound judgment within established priorities and decision-making structures, recognizing when issues, risks, recommendations, or proposed changes require consultation or approval. Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle student and institutional information responsibly while supporting a diverse student population through inclusive, student-centered practices. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in higher education, student affairs, career development, educational technology, instructional design, business, communication, information systems, or a related discipline. Experience in college career services, educational technology, student success, workforce development, or a related higher education environment. Experience implementing or administering cloud-based platforms, particularly career development, advising, assessment, learning management, or student engagement technologies. Experience designing and delivering faculty, staff, or student training and developing implementation guides, learning resources, presentations, or related support materials. Familiarity with system integrations, single sign-on, data reporting, accessibility, data privacy, and responsible use of artificial intelligence in student-facing services. Experience with vendor coordination, technology evaluation, data visualization, program assessment, or grant-supported initiatives. APPLICATION Application review will begin immediately and will continue until a candidate is selected. Candidates should submit: Cover letter expressing interest in the position, resume, and list of three professional reference via email to human.resources@newberry.edu with the Subject Line: Program Manager for Career Development Technologies. Newberry College does not discriminate against any person or group on the basis of age, color, disability, gender, pregnancy, national origin, race, religion, sexual orientation, veteran status or genetic information. Newberry College is building a culturally diverse faculty and staff committed to working in a multicultural environment and encourages applications from people from diverse identities and backgrounds. E-Verify: Currently the college uses E-Verify for employment verification. E-Verify is an internet-based system that compares information entered by an employer from a n employee’s Form I-9 (Employment Eligibility Verification) to records available to the US Department of Homeland Security and the Social Security Administration to confirm employment eligibility. College Employment Policy This job description reflects the general details considered necessary to describe the principal functions of the job identified and shall not necessarily be construed as a detailed description of all the work requirements that may be inherent in the job.  Job descriptions do not constitute an employment agreement or contract of employment, expressed or implied. Unless designated in writing and signed by the College President, all College employees are considered to be “EMPLOYED AT WILL.” Newberry College reserves the right to change, alter and amend job descriptions, functions and duties at the pleasure of the College President or Board of Trustees. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
