    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/CBB2694288FE9606215883F78F64E0A2/jobs/177499": {
      "title": "VICE PRESIDENT OF FINANCE AND ADMINISTRATION/CHIEF FINANCIAL OFFICER",
      "description": "VICE PRESIDENT OF FINANCE AND ADMINISTRATION/CHIEF FINANCIAL OFFICER You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account VICE PRESIDENT OF FINANCE AND ADMINISTRATION/CHIEF FINANCIAL OFFICER Newberry College - Newberry, SC 29108 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply Description The Associate Vice President for Finance and Chief Accounting Officer will play an important role in this work. Reporting directly to the Vice President for Administration, this individual will lead the College's accounting and financial operations, strengthen financial reporting and internal controls, and help ensure that Newberry's resources are managed responsibly and effectively. This is an opportunity for an experienced accounting professional to make a visible difference. The successful candidate will work closely with institutional leadership, mentor and develop a dedicated financial team, and help build the financial systems and practices that will support Newberry College for years to come. The Associate Vice President for Finance and Chief Accounting Officer serves as the College's senior accounting professional and provides leadership for its day-to-day financial operations. The position oversees financial accounting and reporting, the annual financial audit, internal controls, cash management, banking operations, purchasing, accounts payable, insurance administration, and related financial functions. The Associate Vice President will also lead efforts to strengthen the College's financial policies, procedures, and systems, with an emphasis on accuracy, efficiency, accountability, and service. This is a working leadership position. The successful candidate will be comfortable reviewing financial statements, resolving accounting issues, working directly with staff, and developing practical solutions to operational challenges. The position works within a collaborative financial leadership structure, partnering closely with the Chief Business Officer/Chief Operating Officer and Chief Budget Officer. This allows the Associate Vice President to focus on accounting excellence and operational effectiveness while contributing to broader institutional financial planning and decision-making. JOB FUNCTIONS: Financial Accounting and Reporting Lead the College's accounting operations, ensuring accurate financial records and compliance with generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP). Direct the preparation and review of quarterly financial statements for senior leadership and the Board of Trustees. Oversee monthly closing procedures, reconciliations, and general ledger accuracy. Coordinate the annual financial audit, including financial statement preparation, supporting schedules, documentation, and communication with external auditors. Ensure appropriate accounting and reporting for restricted gifts, endowments, grants, and other institutional funds. Coordinate required financial reporting to federal and state agencies, lenders, and other external stakeholders. Financial Operations and Stewardship Oversee general accounting, accounts payable, purchasing, cash management, and banking operations. Lead the development, implementation, and ongoing improvement of institutional financial policies and procedures. Establish and maintain effective internal controls that safeguard College assets, promote accountability, and ensure compliance with applicable regulations. Monitor compliance with financial policies across College departments and work collaboratively with institutional leadership to improve practices. Coordinate banking relationships, debt compliance reporting, and related financial documentation. Oversee institutional insurance administration, including renewals, coverage reviews, and coordination with insurance providers. Work with Human Resources to ensure accurate transfer, reconciliation, and recording of payroll information in the College's financial systems. Oversee the accounting and reconciliation of student receivables, payments, and related transactions in collaboration with Student Accounts. Operational Improvement and Technology Evaluate financial processes and identify opportunities to improve accuracy, efficiency, accountability, and service. Lead efforts to improve financial systems, automate routine processes, and reduce unnecessary manual work. Establish consistent procedures for financial reporting, reconciliations, documentation, and financial transactions. Collaborate with Information Technology and other departments to strengthen financial systems, data integrity, and reporting capabilities. Leadership and Collaboration Supervise, mentor, and develop financial operations staff, including the College's Controller. Establish clear expectations, promote accountability, and support professional development and cross-training. Work closely with the Chief Budget Officer to ensure consistency between accounting records, budget reporting, and financial projections. Provide practical financial guidance to departments across campus, helping colleagues understand and follow institutional financial policies. Identify financial and operational concerns, communicate their implications clearly, and recommend timely, practical solutions. Promote a culture of responsible financial management and stewardship throughout the College. Qualifications EDUCATIONAL OR OTHER HIRING REQUIREMENTS FOR THE POSITION Bachelor’s degree in accounting, finance, or a closely related field. Substantial progressive experience in accounting and financial operations, including direct responsibility for preparing or overseeing financial statements and supporting external financial audits. Strong working knowledge of GAAP, financial statement preparation, reconciliations, and internal controls. Demonstrated experience supervising or leading accounting personnel and improving financial policies, processes, or systems. Ability to manage deadlines, exercise sound judgment, solve complex accounting problems, and communicate clearly with colleagues and senior leadership. Preferred Qualifications Certified Public Accountant (CPA) credential. Significant accounting or financial operations experience at a private nonprofit college or university. Experience leading higher education financial audits and preparing nonprofit institutional financial statements. Knowledge of restricted-fund and endowment accounting, federal and state higher education reporting, and institutional debt compliance. Experience with financial systems modernization, process automation, cash management, and insurance administration. APPLICATION Interested candidates should submit a letter of interest, résumé, and contact information for three professional references to Human.Resources@newberry.edu with “AVP for Finance” in the subject line.  References will not be contacted without applicant’s permission . Newberry College does not discriminate against any person or group on the basis of age, color, disability, gender, pregnancy, national origin, race, religion, sexual orientation, veteran status or genetic information. Newberry College is building a culturally diverse faculty and staff committed to working in a multicultural environment and encourages applications from people from diverse identities and backgrounds. E-Verify: Currently the college uses E-Verify for employment verification. E-Verify is an internet-based system that compares information entered by an employer from a n employee’s Form I-9 (Employment Eligibility Verification) to records available to the US Department of Homeland Security and the Social Security Administration to confirm employment eligibility. College Employment Policy This job description reflects the general details considered necessary to describe the principal functions of the job identified and shall not necessarily be construed as a detailed description of all the work requirements that may be inherent in the job.  Job descriptions do not constitute an employment agreement or contract of employment, expressed or implied. Unless designated in writing and signed by the College President, all College employees are considered to be “EMPLOYED AT WILL.” Newberry College reserves the right to change, alter and amend job descriptions, functions and duties at the pleasure of the College President or Board of Trustees. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/CBB2694288FE9606215883F78F64E0A2/jobs/177666": {
      "title": "Employability Skills Subject Matter Expert",
      "description": "Employability Skills Subject Matter Expert You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Employability Skills Subject Matter Expert Newberry College - Newberry, SC 29108 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Apply Description The Employability Skills Subject Matter Expert (SME) leads the design and development of Newberry College's institution-wide Employability Skills Framework. The SME identifies, defines, and maps workforce competencies; supports employer-informed competency alignment; and develops competency assessment strategies to ensure the Framework reflects employer expectations and workforce needs. Under the direction of the Employability Skills Framework Project Manager, the SME works collaboratively with the Instructional Designer, faculty, program directors, and other institutional partners to support development, integration, and institutionalization of the Framework. The Framework establishes a common institutional structure connecting workforce competencies, academic learning, credentials, career development, employer engagement, and workforce readiness. JOB FUNCTIONS: Employability Skills Framework Development and Alignment Lead design and development of the institution-wide Employability Skills Framework. Identify, define, and document core workforce and employability competencies to establish consistent institutional competency definitions. Lead workforce competency mapping and support alignment with academic programs and Degree Plus certification pathways. Support employer-informed alignment of Framework competencies with employer expectations and workforce needs. Develop and maintain Framework competency documentation and related resources to support consistent interpretation and application across academic programs. Assessment and Integration Develop Framework-level competency assessment strategies and approaches for evaluating attainment of Employability Skills Framework competencies. Provide subject-matter expertise on Framework competencies to inform curriculum alignment and integration activities led by the Instructional Designer in collaboration with faculty and program directors. Support alignment of the Framework with workforce credentials, employer engagement activities, and career readiness outcomes. Collaborate with the Instructional Designer and other institutional partners to support alignment of competency definitions, associated learning outcomes, and assessment approaches. Framework Implementation and Collaboration Collaborate with the Employability Skills Framework Project Manager, Instructional Designer, program directors, faculty, and other project personnel to support Framework development and implementation. Provide subject-matter expertise and guidance to support consistent interpretation and application of Framework competencies across academic programs. Develop and maintain competency definitions, mapping references, and Framework-level guidance that support long-term institutionalization and sustainability of the Employability Skills Framework. Participate in Framework-related project activities and perform other duties as assigned. Additional Information This is a part-time, 0.5 FTE, grant-funded position supporting development and implementation of Newberry College's institution-wide Employability Skills Framework during Years One and Two of the Degree Plus Workforce Readiness and Institutional Capacity Initiative. Qualifications Master's degree in education, organizational development, workforce development, human resources, business, or a related field. Experience in employability skills, workforce readiness, competency development, talent development, career development, or a related area. Experience developing, applying, mapping, or assessing professional, workforce, or transferable competencies. Demonstrated ability to analyze and synthesize information and translate findings into practical competency frameworks, definitions, or recommendations. Experience collaborating with multiple stakeholders to support program or organizational initiatives. Strong written, verbal, analytical, facilitation, and interpersonal skills. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in a related field. Experience developing or implementing employability skills, workforce competency, professional competency, or career readiness framework. Experience with curriculum alignment, competency assessment, or learning outcomes in an academic setting. Experience working in higher education or with academic programs. Experience incorporating employer or workforce perspectives into competency development or workforce readiness initiatives. APPLICATION Interested candidates should submit a letter of interest, résumé, and contact information for three professional references to Human.Resources@newberry.edu with “Employability Skills Subject Matter Expert” in the subject line.  References will not be contacted without applicant’s permission . Newberry College does not discriminate against any person or group on the basis of age, color, disability, gender, pregnancy, national origin, race, religion, sexual orientation, veteran status or genetic information. Newberry College is building a culturally diverse faculty and staff committed to working in a multicultural environment and encourages applications from people from diverse identities and backgrounds. E-Verify: Currently the college uses E-Verify for employment verification. E-Verify is an internet-based system that compares information entered by an employer from a n employee’s Form I-9 (Employment Eligibility Verification) to records available to the US Department of Homeland Security and the Social Security Administration to confirm employment eligibility. College Employment Policy This job description reflects the general details considered necessary to describe the principal functions of the job identified and shall not necessarily be construed as a detailed description of all the work requirements that may be inherent in the job.  Job descriptions do not constitute an employment agreement or contract of employment, expressed or implied. Unless designated in writing and signed by the College President, all College employees are considered to be “EMPLOYED AT WILL.” Newberry College reserves the right to change, alter and amend job descriptions, functions and duties at the pleasure of the College President or Board of Trustees. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/CBB2694288FE9606215883F78F64E0A2/jobs/177657": {
      "title": "Employability Skills Instructional Designer",
      "description": "Employability Skills Instructional Designer You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Employability Skills Instructional Designer Newberry College - Newberry, SC 29108 Apply Apply Description The Employability Skills Instructional Designer provides instructional design expertise for implementation of Newberry College's institution-wide Employability Skills Framework across academic programs. The Instructional Designer coordinates and supports curriculum mapping and learning outcome alignment activities; develops instructional and faculty implementation resources; and facilitates integration of employability competencies across academic and co-curricular experiences. Under the direction of the Employability Skills Framework Project Manager, the Instructional Designer works collaboratively with the Employability Skills Subject Matter Expert, program directors, faculty, and other institutional partners to translate the Framework into program- and course-level implementation strategies. The position provides hands-on instructional design and faculty implementation support to embed Framework competencies within existing courses, academic pathways, and student learning experiences using evidence-based instructional practices. JOB FUNCTIONS: Curriculum Mapping and Alignment Coordinate and support curriculum mapping of Employability Skills Framework competencies across academic programs, including documentation of competency alignment with existing courses and student learning outcomes. Facilitate alignment of employability competencies with student learning outcomes in collaboration with faculty and program directors. Assist faculty and program directors in embedding Framework competencies within existing courses, academic pathways, and student learning experiences. Facilitate integration of employability competencies across academic and co-curricular experiences. Instructional Design and Faculty Support Develop instructional resources, implementation guides, and other materials to support faculty integration of Framework competencies. Provide instructional design expertise for program- and course-level implementation of the Employability Skills Framework. Collaborate with faculty and program directors to develop effective approaches for integrating employability skills content using evidence-based instructional practices. Develop and facilitate faculty training, workshops, and professional development resources supporting implementation of the Employability Skills Framework. Support faculty in aligning course-level instructional activities and assessment approaches with Framework competencies, associated student learning outcomes, and Framework-level assessment guidance. Framework Implementation and Collaboration Collaborate with the Employability Skills Framework Project Manager, Employability Skills Subject Matter Expert, faculty, program directors, and other project personnel to implement the Framework across academic programs. Support consistent implementation and integration of Framework competencies across academic programs. Develop and maintain curriculum mapping documentation and reusable instructional resources that support consistent implementation and long-term institutionalization of the Employability Skills Framework. Participate in Framework-related project activities and perform other duties as assigned. Additional Information This is a full-time, 1.0 FTE, grant-funded position supporting development and implementation of Newberry College's institution-wide Employability Skills Framework during Years One and Two of the Degree Plus Workforce Readiness and Institutional Capacity Initiative. Qualifications Master's degree or equivalent experience in instructional design, curriculum development, educational technology, or a related field. Experience with curriculum mapping, learning outcomes assessment, and faculty support. Experience developing instructional resources and supporting curriculum or instructional implementation. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, academic leaders, and other institutional partners. Strong project organization, communication, facilitation, and interpersonal skills. Preferred Qualifications Experience in instructional design, curriculum development, or academic program support in higher education. Experience integrating competencies, learning outcomes, or related skills across courses or academic programs. Experience supporting faculty in curriculum development, instructional change, or professional development. Experience with competency-based education, workforce readiness, career readiness, or related initiatives. APPLICATION Interested candidates should submit a letter of interest, résumé, and contact information for three professional references to Human.Resources@newberry.edu with “Employability Skills Instructional Designer” in the subject line.  References will not be contacted without applicant’s permission . Newberry College does not discriminate against any person or group on the basis of age, color, disability, gender, pregnancy, national origin, race, religion, sexual orientation, veteran status or genetic information. Newberry College is building a culturally diverse faculty and staff committed to working in a multicultural environment and encourages applications from people from diverse identities and backgrounds. E-Verify: Currently the college uses E-Verify for employment verification. E-Verify is an internet-based system that compares information entered by an employer from an employee’s Form I-9 (Employment Eligibility Verification) to records available to the US Department of Homeland Security and the Social Security Administration to confirm employment eligibility. College Employment Policy This job description reflects the general details considered necessary to describe the principal functions of the job identified and shall not necessarily be construed as a detailed description of all the work requirements that may be inherent in the job.  Job descriptions do not constitute an employment agreement or contract of employment, expressed or implied. Unless designated in writing and signed by the College President, all College employees are considered to be “EMPLOYED AT WILL.” Newberry College reserves the right to change, alter and amend job descriptions, functions and duties at the pleasure of the College President or Board of Trustees. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
  },
